## Laravel (Monolithic) vs Django+React (Separated)

**Laravel (yang kamu biasa pakai):**
```
laravel-project/
├── app/              # Backend logic
├── resources/
│   └── views/        # Blade templates (frontend)
├── public/           # Assets compiled
└── package.json      # npm untuk compile assets

Command: php artisan serve → semua jalan
```
👉 **Frontend & Backend JADI SATU** (server-side rendering)

---

**Django + React (project kamu sekarang):**
```
TA/
├── pos_backend/      # Django (REST API only)
│   └── manage.py
└── pos-frontend/     # React (SPA terpisah)
    └── package.json

Command: 
- Backend: python manage.py runserver    (port 8000)
- Frontend: npm run dev                  (port 5173)
```
👉 **Frontend & Backend TERPISAH** (client-side rendering)

---

## Kenapa Pisah?

**Keuntungan:**
- ✅ Frontend bisa deploy terpisah (Vercel, Netlify)
- ✅ Backend bisa scale independent
- ✅ Tim frontend/backend bisa kerja parallel
- ✅ Bisa ganti frontend (React → Vue) tanpa ubah backend
- ✅ Mobile app bisa pakai API yang sama

**Trade-off:**
- ❌ Harus start 2 server (development)
- ❌ CORS configuration needed
- ❌ Lebih kompleks untuk pemula

---

